    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics is my strong suit. I enjoy physics and chemistry, where math is essential. I find it logical and satisfying, though I sometimes find philosophy and literature too abstract. Being organized and conscientious, I appreciate the structure math provides. It helps me understand the world around me, even if I keep it separate from my more creative pursuits like painting.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Honestly, sometimes my moderate neuroticism makes me worry. But since math is one of my favorite subjects, especially in science, I usually feel confident. I prefer subjects that have clear answers over philosophy. Anxiety might creep in with complex topics, but my high conscientiousness helps me stay focused and prepared rather than panic.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used AI tools recently to clarify concepts for a chemistry project. It helped break down complex formulas and provided practice problems. It was surprisingly helpful and efficient. I appreciated how it gave step-by-step explanations, which aligned with how I prefer to understand things logically before moving to more abstract creative work.",
