    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "Start by finding the first derivative of the function, dy/dx. Next, set this derivative equal to zero to find critical values. Solve for x. Then, substitute these x-values back into the original equation to find the corresponding y-values. These pairs give you the coordinates of the stationary points.",
