    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning, offering tailored explanations and practice problems. They can create interactive simulations and break down complex topics into digestible steps. This benefits students like me who appreciate structure, making abstract concepts clearer without the pressure of traditional classroom settings or the anxiety of difficult subjects like philosophy."
